        "heading": "Limitation on Admission of Special Immigrants",
        "text": "Limitation on Admission of Special ImmigrantsPub. L. 96–70, title III, § 3201(c), Sept. 27, 1979, 93 Stat. 497, provided that notwithstanding any other provision of law, not more than 15,000 individuals could be admitted to the United States as special immigrants under subparagraphs (E), (F), and (G) of subsec. (a)(27) of this section, of which not more than 5,000 could be admitted in any fiscal year, prior to repeal by Pub. L. 103–416, title II, § 212(a), Oct. 25, 1994, 108 Stat. 4314.",
