        "heading": "Effective Date of 2009 Amendment",
        "text": "Effective Date of 2009 AmendmentPub. L. 111–83, title V, § 568(c)(2), Oct. 28, 2009, 123 Stat. 2186, provided that: “(A) In general.—The amendment made by paragraph (1) [amending this section] shall apply to all applications and petitions relating to immediate relative status under section 201(b)(2)(A)(i) of the Immigration and Nationality Act (8 U.S.C. 1151(b)(2)(A)(i)) pending on or after the date of the enactment of this Act [Oct. 28, 2009]. “(B) Transition cases.—“(i) In general.—Notwithstanding any other provision of law, an alien described in clause (ii) who seeks immediate relative status pursuant to the amendment made by paragraph (1) shall file a petition under section 204(a)(1)(A)(ii) of the Immigration and Nationality Act (8 U.S.C. 1154(a)(1)(A)(ii)) not later than the date that is 2 years after the date of the enactment of this Act. “(ii) Aliens described.—An alien is described in this clause if—“(I) the alien’s United States citizen spouse died before the date of the enactment of this Act; “(II) the alien and the citizen spouse were married for less than 2 years at the time of the citizen spouse’s death; and “(III) the alien has not remarried.”",
