        "heading": "Effective Date of 2022 Amendment",
        "text": "Effective Date of 2022 AmendmentPub. L. 117–103, div. BB, § 105(b), Mar. 15, 2022, 136 Stat. 1103, provided that: “(1) In general.—The amendment made by subsection (a) [amending this section] shall take effect on the date of the enactment of this Act [Mar. 15, 2022]. “(2) Applicability to petitions.—Section 204(a)(1)(H)(i) of the Immigration and Nationality Act [8 U.S.C. 1154(a)(1)(H)(i)], as added by subsection (a), shall apply to any petition for classification pursuant to section 203(b)(5)(E) of such Act (8 U.S.C. 1153(b)(5)(E)) that is filed with the Secretary of Homeland Security on or after the date of the enactment of this Act.”",
