        "heading": "Definition of Appropriate Congressional Committees",
        "text": "Definition of Appropriate Congressional Committees Pub. L. 119–75, div. F, title VII, § 7034(l)(1), Feb. 3, 2026, 140 Stat. 571, provided that: “Unless otherwise defined in this Act [div. F of Pub. L. 119–75, see Tables for classification], for purposes of this Act the term ‘appropriate congressional committees’ means the Committees on Appropriations and Foreign Relations of the Senate and the Committees on Appropriations and Foreign Affairs of the House of Representatives.” Similar provisions were contained in the following prior acts: Pub. L. 118–47, div. F, title VII, § 7034(s)(1), Mar. 23, 2024, 138 Stat. 793. Pub. L. 117–328, div. K, title VII, § 7034(s)(1), Dec. 29, 2022, 136 Stat. 5035. Pub. L. 117–103, div. K, title VII, § 7034(t)(1), Mar. 15, 2022, 136 Stat. 626. Pub. L. 116–260, div. K, title VII, § 7034(q)(1), Dec. 27, 2020, 134 Stat. 1753.",
