        "heading": "Limitation on Use of Certain Information",
        "text": "Limitation on Use of Certain InformationPub. L. 109–162, title VIII, § 832(b), Jan. 5, 2006, 119 Stat. 3068, provided that: “The fact that an alien described in clause (i) or (ii) of section 101(a)(15)(K) of the Immigration and Nationality Act (8 U.S.C. 1101(a)(15)(K)) is aware of any information disclosed under the amendments made by this section [amending this section] or under section 833 [enacting section 1375a of this title and repealing section 1375 of this title] shall not be used to deny the alien eligibility for relief under any other provision of law.”",
