        "heading": "Sense of Congress Respecting Consultation With Mexico",
        "text": "Sense of Congress Respecting Consultation With MexicoPub. L. 99–603, title III, § 301(f), Nov. 6, 1986, 100 Stat. 3416, as amended by Pub. L. 100–525, § 2(l)(4), Oct. 24, 1988, 102 Stat. 2612, provided that: “It is the sense of Congress that the President should establish an advisory commission which shall consult with the Governments of Mexico and of other appropriate countries and advise the Attorney General regarding the operation of the alien temporary worker program established under section 218 of the Immigration and Nationality Act [8 U.S.C. 1188].”",
