        "text": "RegulationsPub. L. 103–206, title III, § 323(c), Dec. 20, 1993, 107 Stat. 2430, provided that: “(1) The Secretary of Labor shall prescribe such regulations as may be necessary to carry out this section [amending this section]. “(2) Attestations filed pursuant to section 258(c) (8 U.S.C. 1288(c)) with the Secretary of Labor before the date of enactment of this Act [Dec. 20, 1993] shall remain valid until 60 days after the date of issuance of final regulations by the Secretary under this section.” Similar provisions were contained in Pub. L. 103–198, § 8(c), Dec. 17, 1993, 107 Stat. 2315, prior to repeal by Pub. L. 103–416, title II, § 219(gg), Oct. 25, 1994, 108 Stat. 4319.",
