        "heading": "Deposit of Receipts From Increased Charge for Immigrant Visas Caused by Processing Fingerprints",
        "text": "Deposit of Receipts From Increased Charge for Immigrant Visas Caused by Processing FingerprintsPub. L. 103–317, title V, Aug. 26, 1994, 108 Stat. 1760, provided in part: “That hereafter all receipts received from an increase in the charge for Immigrant Visas in effect on September 30, 1994, caused by processing an applicant’s fingerprints, shall be deposited in this account as an offsetting collection and shall remain available until expended.”",
